# Claim: Core functions a `#run` reaches give the same value against the Core built into jet as against the toolchain tree's Core, at O0, O1 and O2.
# `#run view()` runs Core's generic sort with a user closure whose failure crosses the Core body, Core's tally and a String method while compiling; the program prints that value, then what `view()` gives at run time.
# The `tree` step reads Core from the toolchain tree; the `built_in` steps run without one, so jet takes the Core sources built into it.
fixture: built_in_core_and_tree_core_run_the_same_comptime/input
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step tree_o0: jet run -O0 run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "abc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\nabc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\n"
step built_in_o0: jet run -O0 run.jet
unset: JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT
exit: 0
stdout: = "abc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\nabc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\n"
step built_in_o1: jet run -O1 run.jet
unset: JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT
exit: 0
stdout: = "abc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\nabc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\n"
step built_in_o2: jet run -O2 run.jet
unset: JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT
exit: 0
stdout: = "abc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\nabc after cab|ezd after ez, E_POINT:negative z|core|3|2\n"
